<header><p class="st-kicker">tribal confederation · North America and Oceania</p><h1 class="st-title">Western Confederacy</h1><p class="st-meta">1785 CE – 1795 CE</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">An alliance of Native nations of the Great Lakes and Ohio country that resisted American expansion and inflicted the worst defeat ever suffered by the US Army against Native forces.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-paris-1783">Treaty of Paris</a> of 1783 gave the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-states">United States</a> land north of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ohio-river">Ohio River</a> that its Native inhabitants had never ceded. Building on earlier alliances, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shawnee">Shawnee</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/miami-people">Miami</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lenape">Lenape</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wyandot">Wyandot</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odawa">Odawa</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ojibwe">Ojibwe</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/potawatomi">Potawatomi</a> and others coordinated through councils, with support from the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/mohawk-nation">Mohawk</a> leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/joseph-brant">Joseph Brant</a>, insisting on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ohio">Ohio</a> as the boundary.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The confederacy was a loose alliance of autonomous nations rather than a government, meeting in council and relying on war leaders such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/little-turtle">Little Turtle</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/miami-people">Miami</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/blue-jacket">Blue Jacket</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shawnee">Shawnee</a>. British posts at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/detroit">Detroit</a> and elsewhere supplied arms. It defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/josiah-harmar">Josiah Harmar</a> in 1790 and destroyed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arthur-st-clair">Arthur St. Clair's</a> army on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wabash-river">Wabash</a> in 1791.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>General <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anthony-wayne">Anthony Wayne</a> defeated the alliance at Fallen <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timber">Timbers</a> in 1794, and the British refused shelter at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fort-miamis">Fort Miami</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-greenville">Treaty of Greenville</a> in 1795 ceded most of present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ohio">Ohio</a>. Resistance revived later in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/tecumsehs-confederacy">Tecumseh's Confederacy</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/western-confederacy.jpg" alt="Western Confederacy" width="320" height="311"><figcaption>Image: Drdpw · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:NW_Native_Tribes,_1792.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1785 CE – 1795 CE</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>tribal confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Little Turtle, Blue Jacket, Joseph Brant</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Indigenous religions</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Algonquian languages, Iroquoian languages</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>United States</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Northwestern Confederacy, Northwest Indian Confederacy</dd></dl></aside></div>

